[11] Congresswoman Frederica Wilson suggested Tuesday that people who make disparaging comments about lawmakers online be 'prosecuted.'

[12] The representative from [Florida](https://www.dailymail.com/news/florida/index.html) was visiting the Homestead Temporary Shelter for Unaccompanied Children about 30 miles south of her district when she said she wants to 'shut down' those who make fun of members of Congress.

[13] 'Those people who are online making fun of members of Congress are a disgrace, and there is no need for anyone to think that is unacceptable [sic],' she said while speaking to reporters and demonstrators in Homestead, Florida.

[14] 'We're going to shut them down and work with whoever it is to shut them down, and they should be prosecuted,' she continued. 'You cannot intimidate members of Congress – threaten members of Congress. It is against the law, and it's a shame in this United States of America.'

